-- title:
--   The complete reporting-bank header and payload are preserved below their end
-- statement:
--   Let $h,J,N_B,N_C,g,f\in\mathbb N$, where $f$ is the bank base, $N_B,N_C$ the source lengths, and $g$ the band-size parameter. Fix source value functions $b,c:\mathbb N\to\mathbb Z$ and integer modulus and shift parameters. Suppose memory $\mu$ satisfies the complete shared-bank storage specification: its nine-cell header and all source-pair, occurrence, and level catalogs are stored correctly. Let $e$ be the layout's final allocation end. If $e\le q$ and $\nu(a)=\mu(a)$ for every $a<q$, then
--
--   $$\operatorname{Stored}(\mu,f,h,J,N_B,N_C,g,b,c)\Longrightarrow\operatorname{Stored}(\nu,f,h,J,N_B,N_C,g,b,c).$$
--
--   All modulus and shift parameters are unchanged. This packages preservation of the entire retained bank into one endpoint check.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/c0ldzy17/three-sum-lean/blob/2b639655e07421b9ac743de9090459bab473a7c0/Submission/ThreeSum/SharedReportingBankHeader.lean#L69-L89

